      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the HAL receives an unsupported parameter, it returns an error. This error is caught by the `RETURN_STATUS_IF_ERROR` macro in DeviceHalAidl, which generates a large volume of log messages, leading to a significant increase in CPU load.\n\nNote: These unsupported parameters are intended for the AOSP HAL, not the vendor HAL.\n\nIf these changes raise any concerns, what are your suggestions for improvement?",
      "parentUuid": "7c87ffcb_147eabe5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "e281b308e6a63cb6d824d90331c6c3fd3bb1dbec",
